  "學障：": "Learning disabilities:",
  "學障與聽知覺困難學童聽到『一千』寫 1000，聽到『五十』寫 50，拼在一起變成 100050；或對中間沒有東西的百位不知道該補 0。": "Children with learning disabilities and auditory perception difficulties will write 1000 when they hear \"thousand\", and write 50 when they hear \"fifty\". When put together, they become 100050; or they may not know how to add 0 to the hundreds digit with nothing in the middle.",
  "學障學童逃避借位運算的工作記憶負荷，直覺看到數字就拿大的去減小的，導致減法算出來反而數字變大。": "Children with learning disabilities avoid the working memory load of borrowing operations, and intuitively take the larger number and reduce it when they see it, causing the number to become larger when performing subtraction calculations.",
